o meet  Lula's powerful opponents led by former  president bolsonaro are determined to  thwart his government at every turn  leaving the new president little time to  celebrate Lucia Newman Al Jazeera  Brasilia one of Lula's campaign promises  was to take action on the Amazon  rainforest let's Explore More on that  with Professor Carlos nobre a climate  scientist and Nobel Peace Prize Laureate  he joins us live from Brasilia Professor  Norbert the destruction of the  rainforest broke new records under the  leadership of Jay bolsonaro briefly just  how bad was the deforestation and why  was it allowed to go unchecked do you  think  well good evening Terry and good evening  tour well president bolsonaro former  president bolsonaro  throughout his political career he  always defended a model of development  which would see the indigenous people  the local communities and the Amazon  forests as enemies of Economic  Development he wants to get rid of the  force to replace by pastures by mining  so he encouraged from day one of his  government 2019  increases in deforestation all through  illegality so deforestation excluded  increased more than 75 percent in these  four years the last four years forced  degradation illegal mining land grabbing  all those things really  they were highest in the Amazon for a  long time so that's why I think you know  president Lula has the the the the right  proposals to stop the destruction of  them and and Professor nobre we're we're  told by the experts that the Amazon  rainforest is a vital resource in the  fight against climate change nula says  look he wants to protect the rainforest  but he also knows that agribusiness is a  key component of the economy how can he  balance these two conflicting issues do  you think  well in fact I mean during his this  political the opening uh discourse  earlier today he said something very  important because Brazil has about  1.6 million square kilometers in cattle  ranches and Lula said there's 300 000  square kilometers of Highly degraded  pastures and we can't really move  towards a much more sustainable uh  livestock farming uh really getting a  lot of these areas for reforestation so  Lula has a plan to restore forests in  many of these areas and to improve the  productivity of livestock for me so I  think this is very positive and also the  modern agribusiness in Brazil all over  the world would pay for the so-called  regenerative agriculture Lula has  already appointed well-known climate  activist Marina Silva as his environment  and climate Minister she's expected to  reach Lula's zero deforestation Target  by the year 2030. how difficult though  would it be to achieve this rather lofty  goal and is it even realistic do you  think  well it is realistic because when Lula  was President  uh 20 years ago  in 10 in 12 years  president Lula two terms and then  president Duma deforestation reduced 80  percent in the Amazon so they they know  how to do it it's more difficult now  because organized crime really took over  all these actions in the Amazon but I'm  very optimistic that actually in four  years in his term as president  deforestation rates will reduce too  close to zero let me get a final thought  from you uh Professor I mean many  climate activists will breathe a sigh of  relief now that bolsonaro has gone there  was a real fear wasn't there that the  rainforest as an ecosystem would have  collapsed what is the future for the  Amazon rainforest and will it ever  recover from Decades of Destruction and  mismanagement  yes absolutely uh we all scientists  relate to the Amazon to climate we are  saying for many years the Amazon force  is very close to Tipping Point The  Tipping Point of becoming a highly  degraded open canopy the greater  ecosystems so we have to get to zero  deforestation and then we have to start  a large scale Force restoration during  cop 27 we launched uh Arts of  restoration largest scale of Forestry  restoration Lula is supporting these  ideas largest scale Force restoration to  avoid this Tipping Point Professor  Carlos Norbert really good to get your  thoughts and your analysis thank you  very much indeed sir for talking to  altazira thank you  thank you

